<cem:description lang="en">This lesson "Technological Needs and Negotiation", belongs to "B1.3 Intermediate", English for Specific Purposes course. It is composed of twelve learning objects, that have the following learning outcomes: Understand information about people’s backgrounds in spoken or written documents. Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company. On the other hand, the communicative functions of this lesson are: Organize points in arguments about topics related to Info systemsTalk about things people are supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen Explain the importance of the legal framework for technological negociation</cem:description>
</cem:resource>
